    {% set heading = "How AEGIS PDNS is different" %}{% set desc = "" %}
    {% include "section-heading.njk" %}

    <div class="card" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <p>Cloudflare is strong for global-scale DNS and enterprise traffic controls. AdGuard DNS is strong for consumer privacy and ad blocking. NextDNS is strong for self-service customization. Quad9 is strong for free security-focused recursive DNS.</p>
      <p>AEGIS PDNS is different because it is built around practical security operations: visible resolver behavior, testable canary domains, public feed outputs, and optional SecretChip support for deployment, policy design, and troubleshooting.</p>
      <p>It is not trying to be the biggest resolver. It is designed to be understandable, testable, and usable by people who need a protective DNS layer they can reason about.</p>
    </div>

